# Descriptive Naming and Comments

## Naming

- Use full, descriptive names for functions, variables, parameters, types, and constants — no cryptic abbreviations.
- Names should clearly express **what** the entity represents or does.

```c
// ❌ BAD
int calc(int v, int t);
uint8_t tmp;

// ✅ GOOD
int calculateAverageSpeed(int velocity, int timeSeconds);
uint8_t currentAssistLevel;
```

## Comments

- Add a comment to every function, struct, enum, and non-trivial variable explaining **what** it does or represents.
- For function bodies, add inline comments for each logical step or non-obvious operation.
- Comments must add information beyond what the code already expresses — do not just restate the code.

```c
// ❌ BAD — restates the code, adds nothing
i++; // increment i

// ✅ GOOD — explains intent
remainingRetries--; // one attempt consumed; abort if zero reached
```

- Use `///` Doxygen style for all public APIs and module-level declarations.
